                <pb facs="0500" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg412"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Griscom to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-02-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Griscom reports that the minister for foreign affairs has informed him that
                    the Japanese minister at St. Petersburg has been instructed to present a note to
                    the Russian Government, the full text of which will be presented to the
                    Department by the Japanese minister at Washington, terminating negotiations, and
                    to break off diplomatic relations.)</p>
            </div>
